Emit Phase::Began at the start of a touch scroll so the gesture latches to one node.

The WPE touch recogniser emitted every scroll event with Phase::Changed and the
terminator with Phase::Ended - never Phase::Began. The scrolling tree only latches a
gesture to a node when isGestureStart() (Began || MayBegin) is true, so the gesture
never latched and every wheel event was hit-tested independently. On a page with more
than one scrollable node under the touch point, the motion events accumulated one
scroll controller's velocity history while the Ended event - which arms the kinetic
fling - landed on a different, empty controller, so the fling computed from a single
sample and the page stopped dead (device-traced on franceinfo.fr with per-controller
logging: motion built ctrl A's history to 20 samples, the Ended event armed ctrl B
with 0). Reproduces only where more than one scrollable node is reachable under the
touch, i.e. heavy real sites, never a trivial page.

Send the first scroll event of each gesture with Phase::Began, tracked by a per-gesture
flag reset on touch-down. Latching then binds the whole gesture - Began, the Changed
motion stream, and the Ended terminator, all routed via useLatchedEventElement() - to
one node, and the fling arms on the node that accumulated the motion.

--- a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/libwpe/TouchGestureController.h	2026-07-20 21:45:39.503260687 +0000
+++ b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/libwpe/TouchGestureController.h	2026-07-20 21:46:36.290607677 +0000
@@ -86,6 +86,11 @@
 
     bool m_xAxisLockBroken { false };
     bool m_yAxisLockBroken { false };
+    // True once this gesture has emitted its first axis (scroll) event. The first is
+    // sent with Phase::Began so the scrolling tree latches the gesture to one node;
+    // without it every event hit-tests independently and a flick splits across nodes,
+    // killing the kinetic fling. See webkit-touch-gesture-began-phase.patch.
+    bool m_axisGestureStarted { false };
 };
 
 } // namespace WebKit
--- a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/libwpe/TouchGestureController.cpp	2026-07-20 21:45:39.503260687 +0000
+++ b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/libwpe/TouchGestureController.cpp	2026-07-20 21:48:02.999133714 +0000
@@ -52,6 +52,7 @@
         m_start = { true, touchPoint->time, touchPoint->x, touchPoint->y };
         m_offset = { touchPoint->x, touchPoint->y };
         m_xAxisLockBroken = m_yAxisLockBroken = false;
+        m_axisGestureStarted = false;
         break;
     case wpe_input_touch_event_type_motion:
     {
@@ -81,7 +82,16 @@
         case GesturedEvent::Axis:
         {
             AxisEvent generatedEvent;
-            generatedEvent.phase = WebWheelEvent::Phase::Changed;
+            // The first scroll event of a gesture must be Phase::Began so the scrolling
